{
  "_doc": "THE launcher-icon pattern of the fleet, declared once. Every fleet app's Android launcher icon (adaptive foreground + background + monochrome, ic_launcher and ic_launcher_round, plus any activity-alias icons it declares) is GENERATED from this file by 1_cicd/src/scripts/cloud-android-launcher-icons.py, keyed by the app's own build.json::launcher_icon {glyph, category}. The pattern is the one cloud-tasks, cloud-nav and cloud-browser drew by hand: a 24dp Material glyph scaled 1.917 into the 108dp viewport at (31,35) (≈46dp, centred in the 72dp safe area, nudged down to leave the top-right free), white; plus the shared translucent cloud badge (Material `cloud`, scale 0.62 at (68.6,20.6)) top-right; over a diagonal two-stop gradient. The monochrome (themed icon) layer is the glyph alone. Run `python3 1_cicd/src/scripts/cloud-android-launcher-icons.py` to regenerate, `--check` to verify (launcher-icons-guard.yml).",
  "exempt": {
    "ac_cloud-search": "Keeps its own Phosphor shooting-star icon (owner decision), generated by ac_cloud-search/app/tools/phosphor2vd.py.",
    "aa_cloud-superapp": "Keeps its own hand-drawn icon, the big white \"D\" on black with the cloud badge (owner decision, restored from before the unified pattern); adaptive + monochrome layers live in aa_cloud-superapp/app/src/main/res and are guarded by aa_cloud-superapp/test/test-launcher-icon-own.sh."
  },
